<title>
Klipsch GMX A 2.1 = happyness
</title>
<date>
April 6, 2006
</date>
<reviewer>
Barbara L. Maranville "microangelo"
</reviewer>
<reviewer_location>
Livermore, CA
</reviewer_location>
<review_text>
The Klipsch GMX A 2.1 Has very good clarity for those high tones and VERY good bass for the lows. The small mids & tweeters are packaged very well and sit nicely on most surfaces. I find the added ability of rotation some what stiff but still a nice feature. The system can be played at almost max volume with very little distortion. I play allot of Techno music and find that this system brings out all those sounds I was missing with my last system.
The satellite controller is nice and very responsive to slight knob turning, I still have not turned the bass more than half way for fear my windows will break!
It is truly unbelievable how much great sound comes out of this set up and for such a good price.
I did have a fuse blow on the amp (I still don't know why) but I replaced it and it's still working fine.
I would suggest this system to anyone wanting clear loud sound at a very reasonable price
</review_text>
</review>
